## Solution

### Recommended evidence artifact
Single Google Doc/Sheet in the approved-policies folder (or sibling): **"Equipment Disposal & Re-use Log — [audit period]"**

Per device:
- Device ID (serial / asset tag)
- Type (laptop / phone / external drive)
- Action (disposed / re-used internally / returned to leasing co.)
- Date
- Verification method — pin to NIST 800-88 vocab the policies already use:
  - "Clear" = factory reset (e.g. macOS *Erase All Content & Settings*, full OS reinstall) — for re-use
  - "Purge" = cryptographic erase, valid only on FDE devices (per Data Mgmt Policy Appendix A)
  - "Destroy" = third-party E-Waste service → attach COD
- Responsible person (Asset owner per Asset Mgmt Policy)
- Link to COD or wipe attestation

If zero events in audit period: a one-paragraph attestation signed by the Security Delegate stating no equipment containing storage media was disposed/re-used in the period; the Data Mgmt Policy Appendix A procedure applies if any occurred.

Upload to **both** AST-71 and AST-1 as a Document evidence item in Vanta.

